  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Minnesota has $1.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 26,594 awards with an average award size of $59.5K. Obligations are down 36.4% year over year, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $506M, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $263M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $258M. NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION leads vendors with $185M, and MCGOUGH CONSTRUCTION CO., LLC follows with $106M. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligation at $185M, while Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Cheese Manufacturing reported $127M and $95M respectively. Historical annual obligations show FY24 at $3B as the peak in the last six years, with FY21 through FY25 ranging between $2.4B and $3B and FY26 currently at $1.6B. These figures represent contract obligations only and reflect fiscal year to date totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations are down 36.4% year over year. Award count stands at 26,594 and average award size is $59.5K, reflecting the current FY2026 to date totals. Annual context shows FY25 at $2.5B and FY24 at $3B, with FY26 at $1.6B so far."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate Minnesota federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $506M, the Department of Agriculture obligated $263M, and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $258M in FY2026 to date. NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION received $185M and MCGOUGH CONSTRUCTION CO., LLC received $106M. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing led industries with $185M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $127M and Cheese Manufacturing at $95M."
      }
    ]
  },
